  "body": "Hello lovely humans,\n\n[wdio-mocha-framework](https://www.npmjs.com/package/wdio-mocha-framework) just published its new version 0.3.7.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      State\n    </th>\n    <td>\n      Failing tests :rotating_light:\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Dependency\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      wdio-mocha-framework\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      New version\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      0.3.7\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Type\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      devDependency\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nThis version is **covered** by your **current version range** and after updating it in your project **the build went from success to failure**.\n\nAs wdio-mocha-framework is “only” a devDependency of this project it **might not break production or downstream projects**, but “only” your build or test tools – **preventing new deploys or publishes**.\n\nI recommend you give this issue a high priority. I’m sure you can resolve this :muscle:\n\nOf course this could just be a false positive, caused by a flaky test suite, or third parties that are currently broken or unavailable, but that would be another problem I’d recommend working on.\n\nDo you have any ideas how I could improve these pull requests? Did I report anything you think isn’t right?\nAre you unsure about how things are supposed to work?\n\nThere is a collection of [frequently asked questions](https://greenkeeper.io/faq.html) and while I’m just a bot, there is a group of people who are happy to teach me new things. [Let them know](https://github.com/greenkeeperio/greenkeeper/issues/new).\n\nGood luck with your project :sparkles:\n\nYou rock!\n\n:palm_tree:\n\n---\n\nThe new version differs by 11 commits .\n- [`d6c20ad`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/d6c20ad075a4545cee923e7308efd6416231d459) <code>v0.3.7</code>\n- [`cd94caa`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/cd94caa5743691b698226962afbd6c92b97f8a7e) <code>Revert \"Context for mochaOpts.requires\"</code>\n- [`3cde161`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/3cde1619db460b596ad8bcf8da27657297238b4d) <code>fixed tests</code>\n- [`763f772`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/763f7723cde6201bd56296361401354051707311) <code>v0.3.6</code>\n- [`51c5716`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/51c5716ef82336523f2a77c6e2eb65e5b79736e3) <code>bumped borked wdio-sync version</code>\n- [`ca9bbb9`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/ca9bbb91b123b17e1901abb8e079e19ed78098d3) <code>Update contributors</code>\n- [`3897a4a`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/3897a4ab1253754ac6baab2ae68830be26399304) <code>added tests to cover webdriverio/webdriverio#1456</code>\n- [`cda8776`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/cda8776c9473992fdc73a19ae184e30895b69b2a) <code>renamed mocha require option</code>\n- [`ff40265`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/ff40265923f351d38a7d722cd436b294afda8c17) <code>bumped wdio-sync</code>\n- [`6ebb95f`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/6ebb95f2034b1b5eb871c39d62a1bb7aa19ce6bd) <code>Merge pull request #19 from monolithed/requires</code>\n- [`a1788f0`](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/commit/a1788f05917c80f1baf75eb17668a1764d91d562) <code>Context for mochaOpts.requires</code>\n\nSee the [full diff](https://github.com/webdriverio/wdio-mocha-framework/compare/fbbaada5cefafdd209212f46384b50c551abce59...d6c20ad075a4545cee923e7308efd6416231d459).\n\n---\n\nThis pull request was created by [greenkeeper.io](https://greenkeeper.io/).\n\n<sub>Tired of seeing this sponsor message? :zap: `greenkeeper upgrade`</sub>\n",
